# Worktree responsibility

This checkout is the source of truth for branching Monte Carlo and its
mathematics. Its active branch is `local/mc-tuple-policy`.

- Work here on coding-tree sampling, mechanisms, moment and integrability
  theory, rate or tuple-policy optimization, numerical certificates, proofs,
  Lean formalization, and Monte Carlo label/reference reliability.
- Keep existing neural-network reproduction code working when MC interfaces
  change, but do not start new NN fitting, backbone, operator-learning, or
  latent/Fourier research in this worktree.
- Put new NN work in the sibling checkout `../parabolab-latent-fourier` on
  `research/nn-latent-fourier`.
- When work spans both areas, define the MC producer contract here and make
  the NN consumer change separately in the sibling worktree. Do not silently
  merge or copy unrelated branch changes between the two.
